WEBVTT

00:03.270 --> 00:04.610
Please, Gido!

00:04.610 --> 00:05.780
Stop!

00:05.780 --> 00:07.150
Gido!

00:08.490 --> 00:09.410
Maya!

00:12.030 --> 00:13.280
Please...

00:13.830 --> 00:15.830
Please, save me!

00:17.710 --> 00:18.410
Ozma!

00:26.590 --> 00:27.420
Ozma...

00:48.950 --> 00:51.360
Sam! Are you okay?

00:58.710 --> 00:58.760
LEIJI MATSUMOTO'S

00:58.710 --> 00:58.760
OZMA

01:04.710 --> 01:07.670
You looked over the desert wasteland from above

01:07.670 --> 01:10.880
kareki wo sora de mioroshita

01:07.670 --> 01:10.880
and saw dead trees scattered throughout

01:10.880 --> 01:16.560
aoi tori ga nageki naku to

01:10.880 --> 01:16.560
Blue bird, who knows no sadness

01:17.140 --> 01:20.060
machigai darake no kibou no

01:17.140 --> 01:20.060
I ground my teeth, my hope full of misconceptions

01:20.060 --> 01:25.020
okuba de kanda nigai suna hakidasenai

01:20.060 --> 01:25.020
and couldn't spit out the dreadful sand in my mouth

01:25.020 --> 01:30.150
atoaji wa namida he to toketa

01:25.020 --> 01:30.150
Left was only the salt of tears

01:30.150 --> 01:35.580
aisuru mono sae mamorenai okubyou mono ni

01:30.150 --> 01:35.580
For cowards unable to protect the ones they love

01:35.580 --> 01:41.330
michitarita asa wa konai

01:35.580 --> 01:41.330
no future waits past the dawn of day

01:41.710 --> 01:42.500
Woah

01:42.080 --> 01:42.830
oh

01:42.500 --> 01:43.330
oh!

01:42.870 --> 01:47.800
asu no tobira doko he tsuzuitemo

01:42.870 --> 01:47.800
Wherever the door to the future may lead

01:47.800 --> 01:53.010
haruka misueta me wa nidoto sorasanai

01:47.800 --> 01:53.010
I'll stay focused on what I need to do for it myself

01:53.010 --> 01:54.470
Oh,

01:54.090 --> 01:54.890
woah

01:54.430 --> 01:55.350
oh

01:54.890 --> 01:55.680
oh!

01:55.260 --> 02:00.060
itoshiki kimi no kokoro tataku yo

01:55.260 --> 02:00.060
I will take my place in your heart

02:00.060 --> 02:09.320
itsuka tadashii sekai he kimi wo tsureteyuku kara

02:00.060 --> 02:09.320
because one day I will show you the world we should live in

02:23.410 --> 02:28.170
Episode 4: To the Ends of the Earth

02:32.380 --> 02:35.010
That was... Ozma.

02:35.510 --> 02:36.340
Maya...

02:36.970 --> 02:38.720
Maya called Ozma and it came!

02:41.560 --> 02:42.890
Captain!

02:42.890 --> 02:44.850
Hey, Sam!

02:44.850 --> 02:47.900
How'd you get so much sand inside this thing?

02:47.900 --> 02:49.610
Cool it, gramps.

02:50.150 --> 02:51.860
That's strange.

02:51.860 --> 02:54.360
There's nothing wrong with the anti-sand filter...

02:54.610 --> 02:57.910
Like I said,
I just got sucked inside a QTF!

02:57.910 --> 02:59.330
What?

02:59.330 --> 03:02.700
Theseus has a quantum transition engine?

03:02.700 --> 03:04.290
Yeah, they do!

03:04.290 --> 03:06.500
It was in their newest subterranean craft.

03:06.500 --> 03:07.420
Captain...

03:07.420 --> 03:09.840
More importantly,
Sam, where's Maya?

03:11.090 --> 03:12.510
I couldn't save her.

03:13.760 --> 03:16.720
Theseus took her and ran!

03:17.010 --> 03:18.010
Captain!

03:19.010 --> 03:20.600
It's not too late!

03:20.600 --> 03:22.640
We can still catch them,
and get Maya back!

03:22.640 --> 03:25.480
Mimay, take a look at Sam's injuries.

03:26.100 --> 03:27.020
Yes, ma'am.

03:27.020 --> 03:28.480
Damn it!

03:28.730 --> 03:32.780
I'm gonna bring her back,
with or without you!

03:36.740 --> 03:38.200
Sam!

03:45.000 --> 03:46.500
Get off, Mimay!

03:46.500 --> 03:48.170
How am I supposed to do that <i>now</i>?

03:48.170 --> 03:49.250
Don't ask me!

03:49.250 --> 03:50.710
You didn't ask me when you got on!

03:50.710 --> 03:52.420
Jeez, you're such a kid.

03:52.420 --> 03:54.510
I can't let you go alone.

03:54.510 --> 03:55.550
Shut up!

03:55.880 --> 03:58.510
I can't guarantee you'll be safe, okay?

03:59.760 --> 04:03.010
He's gonna take on Theseus all on his own?

04:03.310 --> 04:05.270
We gotta stop him...

04:05.270 --> 04:06.520
Leave him be.

04:06.520 --> 04:09.560
As long as Mimay's with him,
she'll keep him in line.

04:09.560 --> 04:10.520
But...

04:11.690 --> 04:14.980
What's Sam so hung up on, anyway?

04:14.980 --> 04:16.900
He's turned out like Dick in a weird way.

04:19.570 --> 04:20.280
Oh...

04:21.950 --> 04:24.290
S-Sorry, Captain.

04:33.920 --> 04:35.300
Dick!

04:36.460 --> 04:37.970
Hold up!

04:37.970 --> 04:39.590
Don't be so impatient!

04:39.800 --> 04:42.970
If you won't go, I'll go by myself.

04:45.180 --> 04:48.480
The Goddess of Theseus can speak with Ozma.

04:49.310 --> 04:53.480
I might learn something
that could save everyone... and the world.

04:54.860 --> 04:57.740
She's our last hope.

04:59.030 --> 05:00.070
Dick...

05:05.280 --> 05:06.660
Dick!

05:07.120 --> 05:08.910
Just wait for me, Bainas!

05:08.910 --> 05:11.670
I'll find Ozma for sure!

05:12.920 --> 05:15.670
We're gonna change the world!

05:16.800 --> 05:17.760
Dick...

05:23.430 --> 05:24.510
Captain?

05:26.140 --> 05:28.470
Yeah. He's just like him.

05:29.060 --> 05:32.900
Of course, Dick never found
what he was searching for.

05:36.520 --> 05:40.990
Sam just said that
Maya called Ozma, didn't he?

05:40.990 --> 05:42.320
Y-Yeah.

05:43.360 --> 05:46.830
I just remembered something
that Dick once told me.

05:46.830 --> 05:50.500
The Goddess of Theseus can
communicate with Ozma, he said.

05:51.750 --> 05:52.710
You can't...

05:52.710 --> 05:55.710
You believe what Sam said?

06:12.520 --> 06:13.480
Found them.

06:13.850 --> 06:15.020
I found them!

06:15.020 --> 06:17.400
All right! Let's do this!

06:18.070 --> 06:19.820
No, you idiot! Wait!

06:19.820 --> 06:22.700
Can it! I'm gonna save Maya!

06:24.910 --> 06:25.990
What the hell?

06:25.990 --> 06:31.370
If you really want to save her,
you'd better start listening to me right now!

06:31.370 --> 06:34.870
Do you still not understand
how the captain feels?

06:38.880 --> 06:41.380
I'll open a channel to HQ.

06:42.670 --> 06:44.090
General Danga,

06:44.090 --> 06:46.390
we've secured Miss Maya.

06:47.430 --> 06:50.010
Is there any change in her?

06:51.470 --> 06:52.730
What do you mean?

06:53.480 --> 06:55.350
If not, then that's fine.

06:55.350 --> 06:58.770
General, why did Miss Maya do this?

06:59.730 --> 07:05.610
Miss Maya's ways
are beyond your understanding.

07:05.610 --> 07:08.370
Return to HQ at once.

07:08.740 --> 07:10.160
Understood, sir.

07:20.000 --> 07:22.840
Beyond our understanding?

07:23.670 --> 07:25.630
General Danga must be getting old.

07:26.590 --> 07:30.550
I've known for a long time that Miss Maya
is connected somehow with Ozma.

07:34.230 --> 07:40.940
If I can learn something about Ozma
from Miss Maya, I'll have the upper hand.

07:41.190 --> 07:46.200
His era will end, and mine will begin.

08:00.290 --> 08:01.460
Miss Maya.

08:01.460 --> 08:02.710
Excuse me.

08:07.470 --> 08:09.220
I have a message from the General.

08:10.680 --> 08:13.720
He says we are to obey your instructions.

08:14.810 --> 08:17.350
General Danga said that?

08:17.350 --> 08:17.980
Yes.

08:19.480 --> 08:21.020
He really said that?

08:21.940 --> 08:22.730
Yes.

08:24.070 --> 08:25.230
All right.

08:25.820 --> 08:27.650
Then, send me to the Zone.

08:49.840 --> 08:53.390
They're leaving!
They're gonna escape with Maya!

08:59.940 --> 09:01.440
What are we gonna do now?

09:01.440 --> 09:03.480
We let them get away!

09:03.480 --> 09:05.980
The Captain is just like you!

09:05.980 --> 09:08.030
She wants to save Maya!

09:08.030 --> 09:10.150
Don't lie to me!

09:10.490 --> 09:14.450
I'm telling you, the Captain's been
getting ready to save her this whole time!

09:14.450 --> 09:15.660
What do you mean?

09:15.660 --> 09:17.500
See for yourself!

09:17.500 --> 09:19.080
How am I gonna do that?

09:19.080 --> 09:20.580
Any way you like!

09:27.760 --> 09:29.010
The Bardanos...

09:31.510 --> 09:33.010
That's the...

09:33.590 --> 09:34.640
Monokeros!

09:35.430 --> 09:37.970
Holy crap! That's awesome!

09:37.970 --> 09:40.770
You equipped the Monokeros, Captain?

09:40.770 --> 09:41.940
Yes.

09:41.940 --> 09:46.070
Your brother believed that
Maya could call Ozma, too.

09:46.070 --> 09:46.940
Really?

09:47.320 --> 09:52.360
The only way to catch Ozma is
to take Maya back from Theseus.

09:52.360 --> 09:53.490
Okay!

09:53.490 --> 09:58.330
Captain... Even if we do
get Maya back and call Ozma...

09:58.330 --> 10:02.080
Can we really catch
that huge thing with the Monokeros?

10:02.410 --> 10:03.710
We can.

10:03.710 --> 10:06.000
My brother was sure of it.

10:06.000 --> 10:07.290
I know.

10:09.800 --> 10:13.590
I know more than anyone
how much he had riding on this.

10:20.520 --> 10:21.730
I'll do it.

10:22.520 --> 10:25.350
I'll capture Ozma in my brother's place.

10:41.830 --> 10:44.830
Theseus' ship sighted,
2000 meters off the bow!

10:44.830 --> 10:47.210
Maya, I'm coming for you!

10:52.260 --> 10:53.920
The noise here is terrible.

10:53.920 --> 10:55.300
A sandstorm?

10:55.300 --> 10:56.720
It's very strong.

10:56.720 --> 10:58.850
We can't determine anything
about our surroundings.

11:00.220 --> 11:01.520
Use the magnetic probe.

11:01.520 --> 11:02.560
Roger.

11:12.900 --> 11:14.570
Signal received from probe.

11:14.570 --> 11:16.160
Analyzing.

11:19.490 --> 11:22.200
Metallic object sighted!
2000 meters off the stern!

11:23.250 --> 11:24.500
It's a periscope!

11:25.960 --> 11:27.210
It's the Bardanos!

11:28.420 --> 11:31.340
I wasn't expecting
to catch them in our trap.

11:31.750 --> 11:33.090
High-speed dive!

11:37.800 --> 11:39.430
The enemy ship is diving.

11:39.430 --> 11:40.850
They've found us!

11:40.850 --> 11:42.510
Full power to both engines!

11:42.510 --> 11:43.930
Aye aye!

11:43.930 --> 11:47.390
Quantum transition engine output to maximum!

11:53.030 --> 11:56.150
Listen closely!
Don't miss so much as a heartbeat!

11:56.150 --> 11:58.360
I'll keep my ears peeled!

11:58.570 --> 12:01.160
Captain, won't the enemy see us?

12:01.160 --> 12:02.410
It's fine.

12:02.410 --> 12:05.120
In this weather,
they won't be able to hear anything.

12:05.410 --> 12:07.870
Hard to starboard, full speed!

12:07.870 --> 12:10.250
Roger. Hard to starboard.

12:13.500 --> 12:15.340
While we've got...

12:23.060 --> 12:27.430
The wind's masking their engine sounds.

12:27.980 --> 12:29.900
There's nothing I can do.

12:35.110 --> 12:36.990
Turn off both our engines.

12:36.990 --> 12:40.240
We will now enter anti-subterranean mode.

12:41.280 --> 12:44.660
Load torpedo tubes #1 to #4 with Sandfish!

12:44.660 --> 12:46.290
Sandfish loaded.

12:46.580 --> 12:49.790
We'll use active sonar
to locate the enemy vessel.

12:49.790 --> 12:50.500
Roger.

12:52.330 --> 12:53.920
I can hear engines!

12:53.920 --> 12:55.460
Okay, position confirmed!

12:59.220 --> 13:00.590
Active sonar?

13:01.010 --> 13:03.180
I've confirmed the enemy's position.

13:03.180 --> 13:04.600
Fire Sandfish!

13:15.270 --> 13:16.900
I'm hearing torpedoes!

13:16.900 --> 13:19.820
Fire acoustic decoys at 2 and 9 o'clock!

13:19.820 --> 13:21.570
Roger! Firing decoys!

13:24.830 --> 13:28.910
When the decoys emit their sound wave,
starboard at half speed and turn us around!

13:28.910 --> 13:29.830
Sound wave emitted!

13:33.380 --> 13:34.540
Okay!

13:34.540 --> 13:36.500
Spin us around hard!

14:06.370 --> 14:07.740
Torpedo impact time has passed.

14:08.200 --> 14:09.910
So we missed?

14:09.910 --> 14:12.330
Prepare to fire torpedo tubes #2 and #4.

14:12.330 --> 14:13.870
Get that data updated now.

14:19.420 --> 14:22.170
The enemy's searching for us
as fast as they can.

14:24.840 --> 14:26.260
Follow that pinger.

14:26.260 --> 14:28.140
It was another one-off.

14:28.140 --> 14:29.260
Fire a decoy!

14:29.260 --> 14:30.350
Roger!

14:39.360 --> 14:40.570
We dodged it!

14:40.570 --> 14:42.610
Next time you hear them,
get their location!

14:42.610 --> 14:43.780
I'll try!

14:45.030 --> 14:46.240
Enemy ship sighted.

14:46.240 --> 14:48.200
Prepare to fire #1 and #3.

14:48.410 --> 14:49.580
Fire decoys!

14:49.580 --> 14:50.450
Firing!

14:54.210 --> 14:56.630
Hard to starboard!
Get us behind those rocks!

14:56.630 --> 14:58.170
Hard to starboard!

15:06.720 --> 15:08.850
The enemy's hiding behind the rocks!

15:08.850 --> 15:10.310
Stand by at our present position.

15:10.310 --> 15:11.350
Roger.

15:13.060 --> 15:14.230
Captain, something's wrong.

15:14.230 --> 15:17.770
They know where we are
when they're firing those pingers!

15:17.770 --> 15:18.900
Looks like it.

15:31.240 --> 15:34.120
Enemy ship sighted,
1500 meters off the port bow.

15:36.580 --> 15:37.880
<i>Now what?</i>

15:37.880 --> 15:40.250
<i>The enemy knows where we are.</i>

15:41.880 --> 15:43.260
Use the active sonar!

15:45.050 --> 15:46.380
There it is!

15:46.380 --> 15:47.590
I've got 'em!

15:47.590 --> 15:48.340
Where?

15:48.590 --> 15:52.100
10 o'clock off our port bow!
Distance of 1500 meters!

15:52.310 --> 15:53.970
#1 and #3, fire!

15:55.680 --> 15:57.640
I'm hearing torpedoes!

15:57.640 --> 16:00.440
Kaara! Load torpedo tubes #1 and #2!

16:00.440 --> 16:02.110
Ready #1 and #2!

16:02.110 --> 16:06.610
Our target is at 10 o'clock,
1500 meters off the port bow!

16:10.820 --> 16:13.450
Both engines to half speed! Hard to port!

16:13.700 --> 16:14.620
Say what?

16:21.880 --> 16:24.760
Is she planning on sinking the torpedoes?

16:28.840 --> 16:30.930
Impact time has passed.

16:30.930 --> 16:32.430
So we missed?

16:32.430 --> 16:34.220
Turn us around.

16:34.220 --> 16:35.140
Captain!

16:35.470 --> 16:38.060
They're good enough to dodge my attacks.

16:38.060 --> 16:40.270
They won't simply run away.

16:40.270 --> 16:43.070
Torpedoes! 10 o'clock off our bow!

16:45.650 --> 16:47.690
Starboard engine to full speed.
Hard to port.

16:47.690 --> 16:49.450
Hard to port!

16:52.660 --> 16:54.540
No good. We missed!

16:54.540 --> 16:55.740
Captain!

16:55.740 --> 16:57.080
What's the enemy doing?

16:59.120 --> 17:01.250
They're turning around and going at full speed.

17:01.250 --> 17:02.830
The next one'll be coming soon!

17:03.040 --> 17:04.380
Engines to full!

17:04.380 --> 17:05.340
Roger!

17:05.590 --> 17:07.760
Captain, Maya's on that ship!

17:07.760 --> 17:08.880
I know that.

17:09.760 --> 17:12.930
Those torpedoes weren't to attack them.

17:14.560 --> 17:17.220
They were to sink the Bardanos.

17:24.020 --> 17:25.610
Those torpedoes...

17:27.280 --> 17:30.150
Use the torpedoes' course
to locate the enemy ship.

17:30.150 --> 17:31.030
Roger.

17:31.030 --> 17:33.620
Load #2 and #3 with Sandfish.

17:39.750 --> 17:40.580
Fire!

17:42.750 --> 17:44.080
I'm hearing torpedoes!

17:53.930 --> 17:56.100
Seven seconds until impact.

17:56.100 --> 17:58.100
Six, five...

17:58.100 --> 18:00.100
Four, three...

18:00.100 --> 18:02.100
Two, one!

18:09.650 --> 18:10.570
Sam!

18:20.040 --> 18:21.080
Explosion.

18:21.080 --> 18:22.580
We've hit the Bardanos.

18:22.960 --> 18:25.960
Send the sound of that explosion
to my headphones.

18:25.960 --> 18:26.840
Roger.

18:27.170 --> 18:29.000
We must have hit them.

18:29.000 --> 18:30.590
We did it, Captain!

18:34.760 --> 18:35.640
I knew it!

18:36.090 --> 18:37.430
Captain?

18:37.430 --> 18:39.600
The Bardanos is unharmed!

18:39.600 --> 18:41.640
There was no decompression sound
after the explosion!

18:41.930 --> 18:42.930
Captain?

18:43.140 --> 18:47.110
They hit the torpedoes
that I deliberately mis-aimed.

18:47.110 --> 18:49.440
While they were doing that,
we got the drop on them.

18:49.440 --> 18:50.860
D-Does that mean-

18:50.860 --> 18:53.360
Hurry! Before the enemy uses their pinger again!

18:53.570 --> 18:54.860
Active sonar!

18:55.530 --> 18:56.870
It's here already!

18:57.320 --> 18:58.660
Where are they?

18:59.740 --> 19:00.740
I've got them!

19:01.040 --> 19:02.450
They're directly below us!

19:02.450 --> 19:03.540
What?

19:07.000 --> 19:10.130
Is this what you meant by "sink the Bardanos"?

19:10.460 --> 19:12.510
Enemy depth, 200 meters!

19:12.510 --> 19:16.510
Prepare six depth charges!
190, 195, and 200 meters!

19:17.010 --> 19:17.840
Fire!

19:21.140 --> 19:22.560
Depth charges!

19:22.560 --> 19:23.640
What's their location?

19:23.640 --> 19:25.890
Azimuth 0!
200 meters directly above us!

19:25.890 --> 19:26.600
Okay!

19:26.940 --> 19:28.110
Trim 90!

19:28.110 --> 19:29.270
Engines to full!

19:29.270 --> 19:31.020
90?

19:31.020 --> 19:32.570
We'll slam the ship into them!

19:33.860 --> 19:35.990
Let's go, men!

19:36.240 --> 19:37.990
We can hear the enemy's engines!

19:38.280 --> 19:39.200
What's their course?

19:39.200 --> 19:41.740
The sound's getting louder... they're surfacing!

19:41.740 --> 19:44.450
Turn us around at full speed!

19:44.910 --> 19:46.330
Why are we retreating?

19:46.330 --> 19:48.630
They're going to try and ram us!

19:51.250 --> 19:53.260
Go! Go!

19:56.680 --> 19:58.220
Full speed ahead!

19:58.220 --> 19:59.010
Roger!

20:05.520 --> 20:06.600
Hurry!

20:08.980 --> 20:10.860
Ram 'em!

20:16.190 --> 20:18.200
Hang on!

20:28.000 --> 20:29.080
Where's the enemy?

20:29.080 --> 20:31.130
There's too much noise! I can't tell!

20:31.840 --> 20:33.710
Th-That's...

20:39.630 --> 20:40.970
The enemy ship!

21:18.170 --> 21:20.630
So you're the captain of the Bardanos?

21:30.100 --> 21:36.530
shin'ai naru anata he

21:30.100 --> 21:36.530
I ask you, my love,

21:36.530 --> 21:43.910
since when your heart

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
setsunasa to kodoku no aida

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
has been lost between sorrow and solitude

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
hasamarete kokyuu wo wasureteru

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
where you lost your grip on reality

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
kanashii uta ni tsutsumarete

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
All around us we hear songs of lament

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
namida ga ochiru sono mae ni

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
but before I give in to the tears

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
kizuite anata wo omoinagara

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
I notice the echoes

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
yasashiku hibiku utagoe ni

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
of a gentle singing voice around me

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
dareka wo aishite dareka ni aisare

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
Loving someone and being loved by someone

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
umareta imi ni sotto kizuketa nara

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
is why we were all born

22:36.880 --> 22:44.380
omoi no mama ni koe wo furishibotte

22:36.880 --> 22:43.170
If you realized that too, put your emotions

22:42.170 --> 22:44.380
into your voice

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
anata mo tsuyoku ai wo utatte hoshii

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
and please sing of love with all your strength

22:59.940 --> 23:11.950
Next Episode

23:00.530 --> 23:01.740
What just happened?

23:01.740 --> 23:03.650
The main monitor's busted!

